MODULE tests.unit.platform.remap.runtime_activation.test_runtime_activation

=== owned runtime activation: what « wanted » means ===
  ok   is running and not paused, and nothing else

=== owned runtime activation: Ergopti runs ===
  ok   starts Ergopti's runtime with the user's consent to close theirs
  ok   does not start a second time while the runtime starts or runs
  ok   records and announces a close only when Karabiner's own quit succeeded

=== owned runtime activation: Ergopti paused ===
  ok   stops Ergopti's runtime and gives back the Karabiner it closed
  ok   never starts or restores anything when Ergopti closed nothing
  ok   keeps the record after a crash and gives the Karabiner back at the next pause
  ok   keeps the record when the restore is refused, so a later try can succeed

=== owned runtime activation: Ergopti resumes ===
  ok   reloads instead of starting a second capture in the same Lua VM
  ok   starts again in place when no earlier start reached the capture
